  ('letting-kindness-in', 46, 'When a coworker offers to grab you lunch, say "Yes, please," and give them your order.'),
  ('letting-kindness-in', 47, 'Leave a kind voicemail or message you received saved, and listen to it once this evening.'),
  ('letting-kindness-in', 48, 'Let your partner, roommate or a friend do the dishes tonight without jumping up to help.'),
  ('letting-kindness-in', 49, 'If someone praises your idea in a meeting, nod and say "Thanks" instead of crediting it all to luck.'),
